      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/41/1",
      "text": [
        " عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ:\n۝ وَ دٰاوُدَ وَ سُلَيْمٰانَ إِذْ يَحْكُمٰانِ فِي اَلْحَرْثِ إِذْ نَفَشَتْ فِيهِ غَنَمُ اَلْقَوْمِ ۝\nقَالَ \"لَمْ يَحْكُمَا إِنَّمَا كَانَا يَتَنَاظَرَانِ ۝ فَفَهَّمْنٰاهٰا سُلَيْمٰانَ ۝ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3414 - Jamil ibn Darraj narrated from Zurara, from Abu Ja'far Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as):\nRegarding the words of Allah (swt), the Exalted: \"And [mention] David and Solomon, when they judged concerning the field, when the sheep of the people had strayed into it\" (Surah Al-Anbiya 21:78).\nImam (as) said: \"They did not pass a judgment; rather, they were discussing the matter. 'And We gave Solomon understanding of it\" (Surah Al-Anbiya 21:79)."
        ]
      }
    },
